# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trunk rules (src/gems workstream). /data holds the official competition
# rasters -- training_features.tif alone is 419 MB -- and is never committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/data
/data/
/.cache/
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
scratch/
*.egg-info/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- os / editor ---
.DS_Store
*.swp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# gems22 workstream additions.
#
# NOTE on the two files that ARE tracked under /data: data/derived/feature_names.json
# and data/derived/features.names.json are kept in git on purpose -- they are the
# audit trail for which of the 156 engineered layers existed and which were
# excluded as catalogue-derived (leakage control, flag F-10). Because the trunk
# rule above excludes the whole /data directory, git will not re-include them by
# negation, so they are force-added and any update needs `git add -f`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Large DERIVED external layers (91 MB total) from the gems22 workstream. These
# are predecessor-session products, not deliverables, and each is pinned by
# SHA-256 + DOI/ScienceBase id in the sibling .json provenance file that IS
# committed. The small external layers the holdout depends on
# (derived_sgmc_faults_100m_u8.tif, the GDR CSVs, template-mask.tif,
# qfaults_prior_u8.tif) are deliberately NOT ignored.
assets/external/lidar_scarp_features_u8.tif
assets/external/geodawn_extensions_u8.tif
assets/external/geodawn_rad_u8.tif
assets/external/context_detector_prob_*.tif
assets/external/ens12_*.tif

# Local staging copy of the gems22 submission. docs/downloads/ is the canonical,
# served copy (GitHub Pages one-click download) and IS committed; submissions/ is
# a duplicate written by scripts/05_build_submission.py and skipped by
# scripts/05b_reverify_published.py when absent.
submissions/
